{
  "_id": "6682bd40ba0e94a3c4025b79",
  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "questionLabels": [],
  "question": {
    "text": "If the points of intersection of two distinct conics <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>b</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> lie on the curve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math> times the area of the rectangle formed by the intersection points is _______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "432",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given conics are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>b</mi><mo> </mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo> </mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.</p><p>The intersection point of these conics lie on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p><p>So, putting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> in both the conics.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>b</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mo> </mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>12</mn></math> ( <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>is rejected because curves coincide)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>±</mo><msqrt><mn>12</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>Hence points of intersection are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>±</mo><msqrt><mn>12</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mo>±</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p><p>So, length and breadth of rectangle are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>12</mn></msqrt><mo> </mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo> </mo><mn>12</mn></math>. </p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/12b8723e-aa3a-4ba1-96cb-94ab741d9dfa.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 235px;\"/></p><p>So, the area of rectangle is given by, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>12</mn></msqrt><mo>×</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>×</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>432</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
